DEF sCommTimeTotal EQU $A9F8 ; bank S1 size 4 array PROBABLE [ram4] SRAM bank 1 copy of wCommTimeTotal (C2D8-C2DB, accumulated connection time: frames, seconds, minutes, +1): stored by CommTime_ShowSummary (51:4000, `ld hl,$A9F8 ; ld a,[wCommTimeTotal] ; ld [hli],a` x4, 51:4030, 30 hits in 7 scenarios) and zeroed at every boot by Sram_SnapshotA9F0PairsAtBoot (4E:4658); the only reader is the unreferenced, never-executed Sram_BuildA9F0DeltaBlock (4E:47EB: copies A9F8-A9FB into a report block), so the role of the mirror is inferred from the copy
DEF sBrowserHistory EQU $AA00 ; bank S1 size 1536 array CONFIRMED [ram4] SRAM bank 1 back stack of the browser: six entries of $100 bytes (ring: head index sSram_A9FE = next entry to write, 0-5, depth sSram_A9FF = entries held, 0-6; each entry is a copy of a 256-byte WRAM bank 6 page-address buffer, $D500 for Browser_HistoryPush): Browser_HistoryPush/PushFrom (4C:4B7C/4B81: `ld a,[sSram_A9FE] ; add a,$AA ; ld d,a ; ld e,0 ; ld bc,$0100 ; CopyBytes`, 72 hits in 9 scenarios) push, Browser_HistoryPop (4C:4BC1, 79 hits in 7 scenarios) pops for the back navigation (Browser_PageView_GoBack), Browser_HistoryReset (4C:4B54 `ld hl,$AA00 ; ld bc,$0600 ; FillBytes`, 210 hits in 20 scenarios) clears it; bank 1 selected in the same routines; the wrap 5 -> 0 (4C:4BA8, 4C:4BE7) and the saturation at depth 6 never ran in the natural traces (no scenario reached the sixth push; the deepest pop read entry 1: browser_pages and browser_r2 read AA00-ABFF); the sibling page cache uses A9FC (write slot 0-2) and A9FD (count 0-3) for three 4 KiB slots in SRAM banks 2/3 (Table_PageCache_Slots 4C:4CEA, PageCache_Push/Pop 4C:4C95/4CF6)
