DEF wPaletteFadeFrom EQU $D880 ; bank W7 size 128 array CONFIRMED [ramop9] start colours of a palette fade: 64 colours of 2 bytes in the order of wPaletteBufBg (BG palettes 0-7, then OBJ palettes 0-7). Every fade driver copies wPaletteBufBg here before it starts the fade (Palette_FadeInFromWhite 4F:42B4 and Palette_FadeOutToWhite 4F:4370 in 63 of the 64 scenarios of analysis/coverage_union.tsv, the Slow pair 4F:42FF and 4F:43B8 in 55 and 11, Palette_FadeOutWithTicker 48:46C6 in 47, the masked pair 48:44E0 and 48:4540 in 27 and 11; the black and four-colour variants 4F:4426-452A never ran). PalFade_BlendColor (4F:4083, 63 scenarios, bank 7 only in the 41 bank-observed replays) writes this start colour, unblended, to wPaletteBufBg for a progress word of 0 (4F:411C) and otherwise moves it towards wPaletteFadeTo: From + (To - From) * progress / 256, PalFade_ScaledDelta 4F:4146. After a fade-out it still holds the palette from before the fade: Browser_PageView_GoBack_FromCache 4E:4C8B, MobileDictView_OnA 4C:501E and MobileDictView_OnB 4C:509A copy it back to wPaletteBufBg after Palette_FadeOutToWhite
DEF wPaletteFadeTo EQU $D900 ; bank W7 size 128 array CONFIRMED [ramop9] end colours of a palette fade, same layout as wPaletteFadeFrom (progress $0100 = this colour). PalFade_Start (4F:4166, fill loop 4F:41CA) stores the colour in BC for every colour of the mode: $D900 for all 64 or for the 32 BG colours, $D940 for the 32 OBJ colours, $D970 for the four colours of the OBJ variants that never ran; BC = $7FFF (white) in every executed driver, $0000 (black) in the two black ones that never ran. The masked fades (48:44E0, 48:4540) copy wPaletteBufBg here first and Palette_SetFadeTargetMasked (48:459D) stores BC only for the colours that the mask selects (the mask is the A of the two drivers, kept in hRam_FFB0; bit n is the group of 4 colours n, and only the 8 groups of the BG palettes can be selected). PalFade_BlendColor copies this colour to wPaletteBufBg when the high byte of the progress word is not 0 (4F:4131) and blends towards it otherwise (see wPaletteFadeFrom)
DEF wPaletteFadeLevels EQU $D980 ; bank W7 size 128 array CONFIRMED [ramop9] progress of every colour of a palette fade: 64 words, word n for the colour at offset 2n of wPaletteBufBg; the low byte is the fraction in 1/256 and the high byte is 1 only for $0100; $0000 = wPaletteFadeFrom, $0100 = wPaletteFadeTo. PalFade_Start stores wPalFadeProgress in the words of the mode ($D980 for all 64 or the 32 BG colours, $D9C0 for the 32 OBJ colours, $D9F0 for four; 0, or $0100 for a negative step: the fades in from white start at wPaletteFadeTo and walk back to wPaletteFadeFrom), PalFade_Step (4F:41E0) moves wPalFadeProgress by the signed wPalFadeStep and PalFade_Step_UpdateRange (4F:4269, 213,287 executions in 63 scenarios) stores it in every word of the mode before it calls PalFade_BlendColor once for each colour; Palette_SetFadeTargetMasked stores 0 for the colours its mask leaves out, but the first step rewrites those words too: such a colour does not change because its wPaletteFadeTo colour is the copy of wPaletteBufBg. PalFade_BlendColor (4F:4083) reads the word at $D980 + DE. The four-colour mode (variants that never ran) fills offset $70 but PalFade_Step_FourColors blends offset $60: the two disagree (docs/research/naming2_ramop9.md)
