DEF wPromptTextBuf EQU $D000 ; bank W5 size 98 array CONFIRMED [ramop10] text buffer of the registration and settings prompts in WRAM bank 5: PromptText_Load (00:153D, called through `farcall` by the 14 sites of engine/account and engine/settings, executed in 23 scenarios) selects bank 5 (`ld a, $05 / ldh [hWRAMBank], a / ldh [rSVBK], a`), copies string number A of PromptText_Table (65:567F, 20 strings, the longest 98 bytes with the NUL: PromptText_DoNotUnplug 65:57A7) here with CopyString (`ld de, $D000 / call CopyString`, 00:1567 and 00:156A, bank 5 only in the 17 bank-observed replays) and returns HL = $D000 and A = $05 (`ld hl, $D000 / ld a, $05 / ret`) so that the caller can hand the text to TextEngine_Run (`pop af / pop hl / call TextEngine_Run`, e.g. Account_LoginIdIntro_PrintMessage); overlay: wMail_Work with its fields wMail_InputBank, wMail_OutputBank, wMail_Selector, wMail_InputPos, wMail_OutputBankVar, wMail_OutputStream, wMail_ItemListPointer, wMail_ComposeItem, wMail_KeywordValue, wMail_ErrorFlag and wMail_ComposeState, and the first 62 bytes of wMail_TextBuf1: the same bank 5 bytes are the work block of the mail library during the POP3 and SMTP flows (the two are never in use at once: the prompts belong to the registration and settings screens)
DEF wMailInfo EQU $D400 ; bank W1 size 256 struct PROBABLE [ramop10] mail info record that the mail server screens show (WRAM bank 1, the first 256 bytes of the staging area $D400-$D4FF, laid over wEditBodyBuf and wEditAddressBuf): +0 the 6 BCD bytes of the date (Pop3_TopPoll copies them from sPop3TopSummary: `ld hl, sPop3TopSummary / ld de, $D400 / ld bc, $0006 / farcall CopyBytes`, 54:4B78; MailServerMgr_DrawMailDate 2E:5005 turns them into 12 digit characters in wMailTextScratch), +$06 the source label (CopyString from sPop3TopSourceLabel, at most 20 bytes with the NUL, 54:4B87; drawn by MailServerMgr_DrawMailFields 2E:4EBD through `ld hl, wMailInfo + $06` (engine/mail_server/tidy_screen.asm:421)), +$1B the subject (CopyString from sPop3TopSubject, at most 26 bytes, 54:4B93; drawn through `ld hl, wMailInfo + $1B` (tidy_screen.asm:437)) and +$C0 the sender, which is wEditAddressBuf (54:4BA2: sPop3TopSenderName, or sPop3TopSenderAddress when the name is empty; drawn through `ld hl, wMailInfo + $C0`, tidy_screen.asm:429; the stores of Pop3_TopPoll in engine/mobile/pop3_top.asm spell it the same way); the error path of Pop3_TopPoll (54:49B9-49D4, never ran) fills the source label, the subject and the sender with fixed texts; MailServerMgr_DrawMailFields (7 scenarios) and Pop3_TopPoll (54:4B78, 34 hits in 7 scenarios) run under bank 1; overlay: wEditBodyBuf, wEditAddressBuf (the compose and address book flows use the same bytes as body and address buffers, the mail server flows never run at the same time); no source file mentions wMailInfo together with wEditBodyBuf or wEditAddressBuf: the mail info flows (tidy_screen.asm, pop3_top.asm) spell the bytes wMailInfo + offset, the compose, viewer and address book flows spell them as their buffers
